          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: بیزار",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بیزار — bezār — \"fed up; weary (of something)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وہ روز ایک ہی کام سے بیزار ہے۔ voh roz ek hī kām se bezār hai. He is fed up with doing the same work every day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بیزار (bezār) is usually traced to Persian bēzār, \"weary of, sick of\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
